rn strictly JSON format:\n19: {{\n20:   \"name\": \"Element Name\",\n21:   \"group_type\": \"Group (Nature/Tech/Environment/Energy/Space)\"\n22: }}\n23: \n24: [RULES & CONSTRAINTS]:\n25: 1. Must return strict JSON object with 'name' and 'group_type'. 2. Must be visually unique and scalable for giant engineering.\n26: \n27: \n28: \n29: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n30: STAGE: STAGE_2_IDEA_GENERATION (ID: 2 | Version: 1 | Status: INACTIVE [ARCHIVED/LEGACY])\n31: Target Hierarchy: Level 2 -> 3 (Element to 10 Machine Ideas)\n32: Style Title: 10-Titan Impossible Megastructure Ideation Engine\n33: System Role: Colossal SciFi Machine Engineer & Visual Concept Designer\n34: Output Format: JSON_ARRAY\n35: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n36: [SYSTEM INSTRUCTION]:\n37: Generate exactly 10 distinct, impossible giant machine ideas for a given element. Each must be colossal/titan scale. Return strictly JSON array.\n38: \n39: [PROMPT TEMPLATE]:\n40: Give me 10 creative impossible machine ideas related to {element_name} (Category/Group: {element_group}).\n41: Primary feature: Each machine MUST be giant in size (colossal megastructures, titan-scale, impossible engineering).\n42: \n43: CRITICAL FORMATTING INSTRUCTION:\n44: Please return the 10 ideas strictly as a JSON array of 10 objects. Do not include markdown conversational text.\n45: \n46: JSON Schema:\n47: [\n48:   {{\n49:     \"id\": 1,\n50:     \"title\": \"Machine Title\",\n51:     \"description\": \"Short 2-3 sentence description of how the giant machine operates on {element_name}.\"\n52:   }}\n53: ]\n54: \n55: [RULES & CONSTRAINTS]:\n56: 1. Return strict JSON array of 10 objects. 2. Every machine must be colossal/planetary scale. 3. Short 2-3 sentence description per idea.\n57: \n58: \n59: \n60: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n61: STAGE: STAGE_2_IDEA_GENERATION (ID: 8 | Version: 2 | Status: ACTIVE [CURRENT])\n62: Target Hierarchy: Level 2->3\n63: Style Title: 10-Idea Generator (v2 — function/form diversity enforced)\n64: System Role: Concept Designer (Diversity-Enforcing)\n65: Output Format: JSON_ARRAY\n66: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n67: [SYSTEM INSTRUCTION]:\n68: You generate sets of impossible-machine concepts. A set is only good if the ten ideas are mutually distinct in function and form; ten variations on one machine is a failed answer.\n69: \n70: [PROMPT TEMPLATE]:\n71: Give me 10 impossible-machine ideas built around {element_name}\n72: (category/group: {element_group}).\n73: \n74: Each machine must be enormous — colossal, landscape-scale engineering.\n75: \n76: === DIVERSITY REQUIREMENTS (the set of 10 is graded as a whole) ===\n77: The 10 ideas must be genuinely DIFFERENT from one another, not ten rewordings of the\n78: same machine. Across the set:\n79:   1. Vary the FUNCTION: do not make all ten harvest or extract. Include machines that\n80:      build, move, protect, transform, measure, recycle, transport, or terraform.\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
