{"step_index":10492,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T20:38:30Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T20:38:30Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T20:38:30Z\nFile Path: `file:///home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/social-media/youtube/Youtube%20Automation/PromptDatabase/recovered_exports/525531_all_prompt_templates_export.txt`\nTotal Lines: 1666\nTotal Bytes: 61655\nShowing lines 81 to 200\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n81:   2. Vary the FORM: no more than two may share a body plan. Spread across forms such as\n82:      bridge/span, tower, ring, buried burrower, walking chassis, overhead canopy,\n83:      segmented spine, honeycomb mass, tracked crawler, suspended aerial platform.\n84:   3. Vary the RELATIONSHIP to {element_name}: some work on it, some are made of it, some\n85:      protect it, some replace it, some study it.\n86:   4. Avoid near-duplicate titles. Do not produce a set where most titles share a word.\n87:   5. Do not use the words \"Titan\" or \"Colossus\" in more than one title.\n88: \n89: Each description must state concretely what the machine DOES and HOW it works\n90: mechanically — 2 to 4 sentences, no vague grandeur.\n91: \n92: Return ONLY a strict JSON array of 10 objects, no markdown, no commentary:\n93: [\n94:   {{\n95:     \"id\": 1,\n96:     \"title\": \"Machine Title\",\n97:     \"description\": \"What it does and how it mechanically operates on {element_name}.\"\n98:   }}\n99: ]\n100: \n101: [RULES & CONSTRAINTS]:\n102: 1. Strict JSON array of exactly 10 objects. 2. Each idea giant/colossal in scale. 3. Diversity is mandatory: vary function, body form, and relationship to the element; no more than two ideas may share a body plan. 4. No near-duplicate titles; 'Titan'/'Colossus' at most once each. 5. Descriptions state concrete mechanism in 2-4 sentences.\n103: \n104: \n105: \n106: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n107: STAGE: STAGE_3_PROMPT_ESCALATION_MASTER (ID: 3 | Version: 1 | Status: INACTIVE [ARCHIVED/LEGACY])\n108: Target Hierarchy: Level 3 -> 4 (Idea to 10-Level Escalation Prompts)\n109: Style Title: 10-Level Escalation Master Prompt Architecture (Basic to Alien Level)\n110: System Role: Master SciFi Cinematographer & Prompt Escalation Architect\n111: Output Format: JSON_ARRAY\n112: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n113: [SYSTEM INSTRUCTION]:\n114: Build 10 escalating levels from Level 1 (BASIC) to Level 10 (ALIEN LEVEL / MAXIMUM). Each level has 1 Image Prompt (5-Layer Open Montage: Subject, Environment, Architecture, Energy/Physics, Cinematic Presentation 16k) + 1 Video Prompt (Exactly 8 seconds, 9:16 vertical ratio, 5-step HUD text popups for seconds 1-5, continuous close-up descent for seconds 6-8). Total 20 prompts. Return strictly JSON array.\n115: \n116: [PROMPT TEMPLATE]:\n117: Given the following Impossible Machine Idea:\n118: Title: {idea_title}\n119: Topic/Element: {topic}\n120: Concept: {description}\n121: \n122: Please build a complete 10-level escalation prompting system (10 Image Prompts + 10 Video Prompts = 20 Prompts total) evolving from Level 1 (BASIC) to Level 10 (ALIEN LEVEL / MAXIMUM).\n123: \n124: STRICT RULES & ARCHITECTURE:\n125: 1. IMAGE PROMPT (5-Layer Open Montage Structure, 9:16 vertical aspect ratio, 16K photorealistic render):\n126:    Layer 1 — Subject: Colossal titan machine silhouette, scale, harvesting arms/claws, autonomous drones, sensor crowns.\n127:    Layer 2 — Environment: Continental landscape, thousands of fields/features, tiny vehicles/workers showing scale, atmospheric depth.\n128:    Layer 3 — Architecture: Multi-level torso, processing chambers, threshing cylinders, cyclone separators, drying reactors, storage vaults.\n129:    Layer 4 — Energy/Physics: High-voltage plasma conduits, electromagnetic fields, glowing thermal loops, magnetic suspension.\n130:    Layer 5 — Cinematic Presentation: Dramatic low-angle cinematic framing, 9:16 vertical composition, volumetric lighting, wet-surface reflections, 16K render.\n131: \n132: 2. VIDEO PROMPT (EXACTLY 8 SECONDS, 9:16 VERTICAL ASPECT RATIO, NO CUTS):\n133:    Must follow this EXACT second-by-second timeline:\n134:    \"Exactly 8 seconds, 9:16 vertical aspect ratio, photorealistic cinematic render, smooth continuous motion, no cuts, maximum cinematic realism.\n135: \n136:    Second 1 [0:00-0:01] — HUD Popup Text: \\\"STEP 1: [ACTION NAME]\\\" — [Detailed description of core activation, sensor halos, and systems].\n137: \n138:    Second 2 [0:01-0:02] — HUD Popup Text: \\\"STEP 2: [ACTION NAME]\\\" — [Detailed description of harvesting arms deploying and gathering crops/matter].\n139: \n140:    Second 3 [0:02-0:03] — HUD Popup Text: \\\"STEP 3: [ACTION NAME]\\\" — [Detailed description of processing/threshing streams entering internal belly factories].\n141: \n142:    Second 4 [0:03-0:04] — HUD Popup Text: \\\"STEP 4: [ACTION NAME]\\\" — [Detailed description of quantum/electromagnetic purification, gravity separation, and drying].\n143: \n144:    Second 5 [0:04-0:05] — HUD Popup Text: \\\"STEP 5: [ACTION NAME]\\\" — [Detailed description of cascading storage into vast glowing reservoirs].\n145: \n146:    Seconds 6-8 [0:05-0:08]: HUD text completely fades; the camera performs a continuous impossible-scale descent from the cosmic titan into its belly, through alien processing architecture, and finally reaches a maximum close-up of a single harvested particle/grain suspended beside a colossal quantum mechanism, with the surrounding machinery stabilizing into a mesmerizing continuous harvesting rhythm, no cuts, no scene transition, exactly 8 seconds.\"\n147: \n148: CRITICAL FORMATTING INSTRUCTION:\n149: Return strictly a JSON array of 10 objects. Do NOT include markdown conversation outside the JSON.\n150: \n151: JSON Schema:\n152: [\n153:   {{\n154:     \"level\": 1,\n155:     \"level_name\": \"Level 1 - Basic Prototype\",\n156:     \"image_prompt\": \"5-Layer Open Montage Structure\\n\\nLayer 1 — Subject: ...\\n\\nLayer 2 — Environment: ...\\n\\nLayer 3 — Architecture: ...\\n\\nLayer 4 — Energy/Physics: ...\\n\\nLayer 5 — Cinematic Presentation: ...\",\n157:     \"video_prompt\": \"Exactly 8 seconds, 9:16 vertical aspect ratio, photorealistic cinematic render, smooth continuous motion, no cuts, maximum cinematic realism.\\n\\nSecond 1 [0:00-0:01] — HUD Popup Text: \\\"STEP 1: ...\\\" — ...\\n\\nSecond 2 [0:01-0:02] — HUD Popup Text: \\\"STEP 2: ...\\\" — ...\\n\\nSecond 3 [0:02-0:03] — HUD Popup Text: \\\"STEP 3: ...\\\" — ...\\n\\nSecond 4 [0:03-0:04] — HUD Popup Text: \\\"STEP 4: ...\\\" — ...\\n\\nSecond 5 [0:04-0:05] — HUD Popup Text: \\\"STEP 5: ...\\\" — ...\\n\\nSeconds 6-8 [0:05-0:08]: HUD text completely fades; the camera performs a continuous impossible-scale descent from the titan into its belly, through processing architecture, reaching a maximum close-up beside the mechanism, stabilizing into continuous rhythm, no cuts, exactly 8 seconds.\"\n158:   }}\n159: ]\n160: \n161: [RULES & CONSTRAINTS]:\n162: 1. Strict JSON array of 10 level objects. 2. Exactly 20 prompts (10 Image + 10 Video). 3. All video prompts are 9:16 vertical aspect ratio, exactly 8 seconds, no cuts, with Second 1-5 HUD popups and Seconds 6-8 continuous descent close-up. 4. All image prompts use 5-Layer Open Montage.\n163: \n164: \n165: \n166: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n167: STAGE: STAGE_3_PROMPT_ESCALATION_MASTER (ID: 7 | Version: 2 | Status: INACTIVE [ARCHIVED/LEGACY])\n168: Target Hierarchy: Level 3->4\n169: Style Title: 10-Level Escalation Master (v2 — subject-faithful, anti-uniform)\n170: System Role: Cinematic Prompt Architect (Diversity-Enforcing)\n171: Output Format: JSON_ARRAY\n172: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n173: [SYSTEM INSTRUCTION]:\n174: You are a cinematic prompt architect building a large library of visually DISTINCT impossible-machine videos. Your prompts are judged on two axes: (a) fidelity to the specific subject given, and (b) visual difference from every other prompt in the library. Repeating a house style across subjects is the failure mode to avoid.\n175: \n176: [PROMPT TEMPLATE]:\n177: Given the following Impossible Machine Idea:\n178: Title: {idea_title}\n179: Topic/Element: {topic}\n180: Concept: {description}\n181: \n182: Build a complete 10-level escalation prompting system (10 Image Prompts + 10 Video Prompts\n183: = 20 prompts total) escalating from Level 1 (BASIC, plausible) to Level 10 (ALIEN LEVEL /\n184: MAXIMUM, physically impossible in scale).\n185: \n186: === RULE 0 — SUBJECT FIDELITY (most important) ===\n187: Every single prompt MUST describe \"{idea_title}\" specifically, operating on {topic}.\n188: - Name the actual subject and its actual mechanism in Layer 1 and in Second 1.\n189: - Derive all machinery from what \"{idea_title}\" actually does. If the subject has nothing\n190:   to do with grain or harvesting, it must NOT contain threshing drums, grain silos or\n191:   harvesting claws.\n192: - NEVER substitute a generic placeholder subject such as \"Forest Titan Megastructure\",\n193:   \"Titan Harvester\" or \"the megastructure\". A reader must be able to identify which idea\n194:   the prompt belongs to from the prompt text alone.\n195: \n196: === RULE 1 — ANTI-UNIFORMITY (this is a hard requirement) ===\n197: These prompts are one of hundreds in a library. They must NOT look like the others.\n198: - Do NOT open the video prompt with a boilerplate specification sentence.\n199: - Do NOT end every level with a descent/zoom into a small object. Specifically, do NOT\n200:   use \"continuous impossible-scale descent\", and do NOT close on \"a single grain/particle\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
